node_modules/
dist/
.env
# Personal machine overrides. `.env.test` itself is COMMITTED — it is the
# suite's shared, reviewable environment — but `*.local` never is.
*.local
coverage/
.DS_Store
*.tsbuildinfo
.kickjs/
# React Router's generated route types (ADR 0044). Regenerated by
# `react-router typegen`, which `typecheck` runs first.
.react-router/

# Astro's generated types and build output.
.astro/

# The server's runtime uploads. Unanchored, this read `data/` and matched the
# examples' `data/*.yaml` — the rows of the reference marketplace — so the site
# the README points at was published with no content in it.
apps/engine/data/
# Copied from install/ at build time — one source of truth.
apps/marketing/public/install/

# Assembled into `packages/server` at pack time from three other packages —
# built output, never edited by hand (ADR 0046).
packages/server/app/
packages/server/migrations/

# Working notes, kept out of the public repository on purpose (they stay on
# disk, they are just not published). `docs/decisions/` is the reasoning behind
# the design and `research/` is what that reasoning argues from — a reader wants
# the product and the code, not the thinking that got here. `FINDINGS.md` beside
# an example is the same thing: a review of what the reference site exposed.
#
# The code still cites them ("ADR 0009 §3"), because a comment that says *why*
# is worth more than a link that resolves.
#
# Anchored to the root: an unanchored `docs/` matched
# `apps/marketing/src/pages/docs/`, so the marketing site's own documentation
# was silently untracked — including the reference page and everything added to
# it. A published page that only exists on one laptop is worse than no page.
/docs/
/research/
examples/*/FINDINGS.md
